{#
compose/_unschedule.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Answer to POST /compose/unschedule/{id}: the row that was clicked, redrawn
without its hold, plus a toast saying so.

`replace` on the row's own id, exactly as thread/status/_star.stream.html.twig
does — the list rows are patched one at a time and never reloaded whole, and
the row carries its own Stimulus controller, so replacing the <li> re-connects
it rather than leaving a dead badge behind.

The include is NOT `only`: _thread_row.html.twig reads `accounts` (the account
wedge is drawn only on a multi-account install) off the globals, the same way
the star and read streams reach it.

Variables: row (MessageThread|Message), type ('thread'|'message'),
           draft_scope (bool), cancelled (bool — false when the mail had
           already gone out, in which case nothing was written)
#}
<turbo-stream action="replace" target="thread_{{ row.id }}">
    <template>
        {% if 'thread' == type %}
            {% include '_partials/_thread_row.html.twig' with {
                thread:      row,
                draft_scope: draft_scope,
            } %}
        {% else %}
            {% include '_partials/_thread_row.html.twig' with {
                message:     row,
                draft_scope: draft_scope,
            } %}
        {% endif %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>

{# Silent on a message that had already gone: the row redraws itself into the
   truth, and "cancelled" would be the one thing that did not happen. #}
{% if cancelled %}
    <turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
        <template>
            {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
                type:    'info',
                message: 'toast.schedule_cancelled'|trans,
            } only %}
        </template>
    </turbo-stream>
{% endif %}
